==English==
{{wikipedia|Tea party (social_gathering)|Tea party}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A semi-formal [[afternoon]] [[social]] [[gathering]] at which [[tea]], [[sandwich]]es and [[cake]]s are served.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 July 1|title=Case Studies: Brew Monday|journal=Rail|page=59|text=On January 23, MTR Elizabeth Line held an office-based '''tea party''' at which colleagues were encouraged to donate home-baked goods. It provided staff with an opportunity to take time out of their busy schedules and reminded everyone to take care of their mental health and wellbeing.}}
# A type of [[imaginative]] [[play]]ing in which [[children]] gather with each other or their [[doll]]s to [[mimic]] having a real tea party or other formal meal, often without any food at all.
# {{lb|en|metaphorical}} An interaction characterized by a high degree of courtesy, delicacy, and the avoidance of conflict.

